 'protocol': {'committed_utc': '2026-09-11',
              'eligibility': 'Included iff ALL hold: a randomised controlled trial; population (in title/registry '
                             "conditions) mentions one of ['atrial fibrillation', 'nonvalvular atrial fibrillation', "
                             "'non-valvular atrial fibrillation']; and none of ['mechanical heart valve', 'mechanical "
                             "heart valves', 'valvular heart disease', 'mitral stenosis', 'heart valve', 'venous "
                             "thromboembolism', 'deep-vein thrombosis', 'deep vein thrombosis', 'pulmonary embolism', "
                             "'acute coronary', 'antiphospholipid', 'catheter ablation', 'ablation', 'cardioversion', "
                             "'device procedures', 'left atrial appendage', 'postoperative', 'perioperative']; "
                             "randomised intervention is one of ['dabigatran', 'rivaroxaban', 'apixaban', 'edoxaban', "
                             "'direct oral anticoagulant', 'direct oral anticoagulants', 'DOAC', 'DOACs', 'NOAC', "
                             "'NOACs', 'non-vitamin K antagonist oral anticoagulant', 'non-vitamin K antagonist oral "
                             "anticoagulants', 'DU-176b', 'DU 176b', 'BIBR 1048', 'BIBR1048', 'BAY 59-7939', "
                             "'BMS-562247'] (named in title/conditions); a comparator among ['warfarin', 'vitamin K "
                             "antagonist', 'vitamin k antagonist', 'VKA']. Excluded (rule id + verbatim span on each "
                             'record): X1 not an RCT · X2 wrong/off-topic population · X3 wrong '
                             'intervention/comparator.',
              'method_declared': 'Random-effects inverse-variance on the log ratio (log RR/OR/HR/IRR as configured for '
                                 'the outcome); Paule-Mandel tau^2; HKSJ 95% CI on t_{k-1} (variance floor '
                                 'max(1,Q/(k-1))); prediction interval mu +/- t_{k-1}*sqrt(tau2+se^2). Validated vs '
                                 'metafor 5.0.1 (this canonical code path; every rendered interval is gate-checked to '
                                 'originate here).',
              'sha': '876acb8be1d610715286042396952dccb50942e1',
              'text': '# Protocol - direct oral anticoagulants versus warfarin for stroke prevention in atrial '
                      'fibrillation\n'
                      '\n'
                      '**Registration.** The commit adding this file registers the review; its SHA is embedded\n'
                      "in the page's Protocol tab and Reproducibility tab. The protocol is committed before\n"
                      'the synthesis is run.\n'
                      '\n'
                      '## PICO\n'
                      '- **P** - adults with non-valvular atrial fibrillation treated for stroke prevention.\n'
                      '- **I** - a direct oral anticoagulant: dabigatran, rivaroxaban, apixaban, or edoxaban.\n'
                      '- **C** - warfarin or other vitamin K antagonist anticoagulation.\n'
                      '- **O (primary)** - stroke or systemic embolism.\n'
                      '- **O (harms)** - major bleeding.\n'
                      '\n'
                      '## Estimand / population / timepoint\n'
                      '- **Estimand** - ratio-scale effect, labelled HR when trials report hazard ratios and RR\n'
                      '  when the trial abstract reports a relative risk.\n'
                      '- **Population** - intention-to-treat as randomised where the trial abstract reports it.\n'
                      '- **Timepoint** - trial end / longest reported follow-up in the pivotal trial abstract.\n'
                      '\n'
                      '## Amendment 2026-09-12 (POST-HOC — dose/analysis selection rule, added after trial data were '
                      'known)\n'
                      '**Status: retrospective.** This rule was NOT in the protocol at the original registration SHA; '
                      'it\n'
                      'is recorded here as a dated amendment so the analysis is labelled post-amendment, not presented '
                      'as\n'
                      'prespecified. It formalises what the pooled analysis already does and aligns with the '
                      'registered\n'
                      'comparator, which is the **standard-dose** DOAC-vs-warfarin comparison (Carnicelli 2022, '
                      'standard-dose\n'
                      'HR 0.81).\n'
                      '- **Dose rule.** For a multi-dose trial, pool the **approved/marketed higher dose** vs '
                      'warfarin, not\n'
                      '  the lower dose: dabigatran **150 mg** (RE-LY, not the 110 mg arm), edoxaban **60 mg** '
                      'high-dose\n'
                      '  (ENGAGE AF-TIMI 48, not the 30 mg arm). Rationale: the higher dose is the licensed '
                      'stroke-prevention\n'
                      '  regimen and matches the standard-dose comparator.\n'
                      '- **Analysis-set rule.** Use the **intention-to-treat** estimate to match the ITT basis of '
                      'ROCKET-AF\n'
                      '  and ARISTOTLE in the pool (ENGAGE high-dose ITT HR 0.87, not the on-treatment 0.79).\n'
                      '- **Confidence-level rule.** Where a trial reports a non-95% CI (ENGAGE 97.5%), recover the '
                      'log-scale\n'
                      '  SE at the **stated** level before pooling; the conversion is disclosed on the row.\n'
                      '\n'
                      '## Eligibility - on P/I/C/DESIGN ONLY\n'
                      'Include a record iff all hold:\n'
                      '- **I1** - randomised controlled trial;\n'
                      '- **I2** - population is atrial fibrillation, judged from title or registry conditions;\n'
                      '- **I3** - direct oral anticoagulant versus warfarin / vitamin K antagonist comparator;\n'
                      '- **design** - randomised DOAC-vs-warfarin allocation; double-blinding is not required.\n'
                      '\n'
                      'Exclude (reason must be true of the record):\n'
                      '- **X1** - not an RCT (review, guideline, observational, protocol-only);\n'
                      '- **X2** - wrong population (e.g. mechanical heart valves, venous thromboembolism,\n'
                      '  antiphospholipid syndrome, catheter ablation, cardioversion, device-procedure studies);\n'
                      '- **X3** - wrong intervention/comparison (no direct oral anticoagulant versus\n'
                      '  warfarin / vitamin K antagonist contrast);\n'
                      '- **X5** - off-topic: a primary trial of another disease/topic in this set (negative control).\n'
                      '\n'
                      '> **Eligibility is NOT on the outcome axis.** Whether a trial reports stroke or systemic\n'
                      '> embolism, or gives a 2x2 table versus only an effect+CI, is recorded as target-result\n'
                      '> status at extraction - never as an exclusion. A published effect + CI is a poolable\n'
                      '> input when the fixed extractor can corroborate it from the abstract.\n'
                      '\n'
                      '## Search (fetch-once; raw results committed under cache/<slug>/records.json; screening replays '
                      'offline)\n'
                      '- PubMed: UID searches for the four pivotal direct DOAC-vs-warfarin AF RCTs: RE-LY,\n'
                      '  ROCKET AF, ARISTOTLE, and ENGAGE AF-TIMI 48.\n'
                      '- ClinicalTrials.gov: condition "atrial fibrillation", intervention "edoxaban warfarin".\n'
                      '- Comparator-reference seeding is disabled because the resolved 2022 IPD/NMA cites later\n'
                      '  subgroup publications that share NCT IDs with the pivotal trials; the UID searches\n'
                      '  intentionally preserve the primary trial abstracts as the extraction source.\n'
                      '\n'
                      '## Synthesis method (DECLARED; served method must equal this - gate limb 1)\n'
                      'Random-effects inverse-variance on log ratio effects; **Paule-Mandel** tau^2; **HKSJ**\n'
                      '95% CI on `t_{k-1}` with variance floor `max(1, Q/(k-1))`; prediction interval\n'
                      '`mu +/- t_{k-1}*sqrt(tau^2+se^2)`. 0.5 continuity correction to all four cells of a\n'
                      'study only if it has a zero cell. DerSimonian-Laird forbidden. Engine validated vs\n'
                      'metafor 5.0.1 (<1e-6).\n'
                      '\n'
                      'This topic is network-shaped in the literature, but this harness synthesis is explicitly\n'
                      'the direct pairwise DOAC-vs-warfarin comparison. No indirect treatment comparison or\n'
                      'network estimate is calculated by the harness.\n'
                      '\n'
                      '## Comparator (resolved; open-access confirmed)\n'
                      'Carnicelli et al., *Circulation* 2022, "Direct Oral Anticoagulants Versus Warfarin in\n'
                      'Patients With Atrial Fibrillation: Patient-Level Network Meta-Analyses of Randomized\n'
                      'Clinical Trials With Interaction Testing by Age and Sex" (PMID 34985309, PMCID\n'
                      'PMC8800560, DOI 10.1161/CIRCULATIONAHA.121.056355; Unpaywall is_oa=true). It reports\n'
                      'standard-dose DOAC versus warfarin for stroke or systemic embolism as HR 0.81\n'
                      '(95% CI 0.74-0.89), and reports major bleeding.\n'
                      '\n'
                      'Ruff et al. 2014 in *Lancet* was checked because it is the classic direct trial-level\n'
                      'meta-analysis (PMID 24315724, DOI 10.1016/S0140-6736(13)62343-0), but Unpaywall reported\n'
                      'is_oa=false, so it was not used as the comparator.\n'
                      '\n'
                      '## Controls\n'
                      '- **Positive** - the search must recover and include RE-LY (PMID 19717844), ROCKET AF\n'
                      '  (PMID 21830957), and ARISTOTLE (PMID 21870978).\n'
                      '- **Negative** - RE-ALIGN, dabigatran versus warfarin in mechanical heart valves\n'
                      '  (PMID 23991661), must be recovered and excluded as the wrong population.\n'},
